# Optional: where the SSO page opens, if the default browser is wrong — a work profile
# rather than a personal one, say. Leave this file out to use the default browser.
# Either way the login prints its URL, so a browser that never opens is not a dead end.
#
# Either an account address, resolved to the profile signed in as it, in whichever
# Chromium browser has it (Chrome, Chrome Beta/Canary, Brave, Edge, Vivaldi, Arc):
# you@work.example
#
# ...or a command, for any other browser. The login URL is appended to it:
# open -na "Google Chrome" --args --profile-directory="Profile 2"
# /Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome --profile-directory="Profile 2"
# open -na "Firefox" --args -P work
